!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-namespace-type-declaring-a-field-beside-its-facets-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2"
  description: """
    A value of a namespace type is the map its `key_type` and `value_type` describe, and nothing else.
    `interfaces` declares `extends` beside those facets, which no value of it can carry: a field there is
    dead, so the meta layer declaring it fails to load. A construct with fields of its own is a record
    holding them, held under a key of a namespace type.
    """
  meta: "meta-kernel.tn"
  import: ["meta.tn"]
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
